# Regatta on __CLUSTER_NAME__ cluster

Workload: Regatta distributed database via custom Regatta Operator
Version: __REGATTA_VERSION__
RDB Replicas: __REPLICAS__
Block Storage: __STORAGE_SIZE__
DB nodes: __DB_NODE_COUNT__
Region: __REGION__

## Endpoints

- **Internal Cluster DNS**:
  - SM: `regatta-sm.__NAMESPACE__.svc.cluster.local:8840`
  - RDB Service: `regatta-rdb.__NAMESPACE__.svc.cluster.local:8850`
  - RDB Pods: `regatta-rdb-0.__NAMESPACE__.svc.cluster.local:8850`, `regatta-rdb-1.__NAMESPACE__.svc.cluster.local:8850`, ...

- **NodePort Exposure** (via node public/private IP):
  - SM: `http://<db-node-ip>:30840`
  - RDB: `<db-node-ip>:30850`

## Lifecycle

```bash
# Install CRD and Operator (configure block device & size if needed)
easy-db-lab kit install regatta --size 500Gi --rdb-device /dev/loop0

# Start Regatta Cluster (applies PVs, CR, and NodePort service)
easy-db-lab regatta start

# Stop Regatta Cluster (keeps PV data intact)
easy-db-lab regatta stop

# Restart Regatta Cluster
easy-db-lab regatta start

# Uninstall Regatta and delete PVs
easy-db-lab regatta uninstall
# Or bypass confirmation prompt:
easy-db-lab regatta uninstall --force-uninstall
```

## Running Benchmarks Inside K3s

Launch a test runner pod inside the cluster (pointing to internal service DNS):

```bash
kubectl apply -f test-runner-pod.yaml -n __NAMESPACE__
```
